# NOTE: this file does NOT stop the dev-watcher rebuild loop — nothing can.
#
# Measured: the watcher reports "File src-tauri/<dir> changed" while that
# directory's mtime is DAYS old and no file in the repo has been modified. The
# events are spurious, and the reported directory just moves to whichever one is
# still watched as you add ignore lines (resources -> src -> ...). An ignore
# rule filters a path; it cannot filter an event about a file that never
# changed. The fix is `tauri dev --no-watch` — `npm run dev`. See package.json.
#
# A real file change still names the FILE ("src-tauri/src/lib.rs changed"); the
# spurious ones name the DIRECTORY. That is how to tell them apart.
#
# What remains below is genuine hygiene, and it matters for a second reason: a
# custom .taurignore REPLACES Tauri's built-in list, so the defaults have to be
# restated or `npm run dev:watch` loops on cargo's own output.
target/
gen/
.git/
resources/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
